linux-sunfish (7.2.8-sm7150-20261107.1+git9a66fdc0d7fd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * misc: fpc1020: shut the trustlet down on remove. Adds
    qcom_scm_qseecom_app_shutdown(); without it the FPC TA stays resident
    after rmmod and the next load fails with -22 until a reboot.
    Hardware-tested on a Pixel 4a: load, rmmod, reload works.
  * Includes 20261106.3 (QRTR early-packet fix).

 -- Miroslav Mraz <mraz.miro@seznam.cz>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

linux-sunfish (7.2.8-sm7150-20261106.3+git9a66fdc0d7fd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * net: qrtr: smd: queue packets that arrive before probe completes. A
    remote that speaks as soon as its channel opens could lose its first
    packets; on a Pixel 4a one boot came up without the ADSP audio services
    (no sound card). Hardware-tested: 4 clean boots, and a qrtr_smd reload
    storm queued (not dropped) an early modem packet; services recovered.
  * Includes 20261106.1 (FastRPC fixes, Titan 170 PIX path + controls).

 -- Miroslav Mraz <mraz.miro@seznam.cz>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

linux-sunfish (7.2.8-sm7150-20261106.1+git9a66fdc0d7fd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * CAMSS Titan 170 PIX: red/blue white-balance and gamma controls on the
    PIX video node (defaults keep the fixed unity/linear pipeline).
    Hardware-tested on a Pixel 4a: grey-world gains + gamma 2.2 give a
    neutral, correctly toned frame; no faults.
  * Includes 20261105.2 (FastRPC fixes, PIX path; both hardware-tested).

 -- Miroslav Mraz <mraz.miro@seznam.cz>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

linux-sunfish (7.2.8-sm7150-20261105.2+git9a66fdc0d7fd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * FastRPC: sync fd-backed buffers around invocations and fall back to the
    legacy INIT_MMAP (both from the A52q port) for CDSP offload.
  * CAMSS: experimental Titan 170 PIX path (CSID IPP -> VFE NV12), enabled
    for SM7150 behind qcom_camss.titan170_pix (default off).
  * Test build: not yet verified on hardware.

